  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>B</mi></math> and <math><mi>C</mi></math> are the points of intersection of the parabola <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The perimeter (in units) of the triangle <math><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is the origin, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "On solving <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br />we get,&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;(as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is rejected because it makes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;not defined)<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0086_d7cf2e786efe.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.92014in;height:1.59375in\" /><br />Now, perimeter of <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units"
  }
